    "knowledge_point": "Graphing a Stretched Negative Reciprocal Function",
    "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of $y=-\\frac{1}{4x}?$",
    "worked_solution": "To plot $y=-\\frac{1}{4x},$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=-\\frac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13831126/assets/9da0db2e6c97e507e82b7ca801e46802fabf91ad31ff53ad3cc9ae580151370a.png)\n\n- Stretch the result by a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{4}$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=-\\frac{1}{4x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13831126/assets/344a3615421b88df05cb666ca90395991f3aa6af75c9095a60c73be89124b7e9.png)",
